From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: ask the firmware only about stations it
 has

mt7915_sta_statistics() asked the firmware for the rx rate of whatever
station mac80211 named. mac80211 also asks about one the firmware
doesn't have: for the last statistics of every removal, after the
station was disconnected; for one not associated yet; and after a full
reset for one not re-added yet, whose index may be another station's by
then. That was a round trip under the device mutex for nothing, or for
another station's rate.

Ask only for an associated station (wcid.sta). The tx rate and the
counters the driver keeps are reported as before.

mt7915_main_test_sta_statistics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/main.c            | 10 +++++++++-
 mt7915/tests/main-test.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/main.c b/mt7915/main.c
index 89b6bc5d..722d2ead 100644
--- a/mt7915/main.c
+++ b/mt7915/main.c
@@ -1291,7 +1291,15 @@ static void mt7915_sta_statistics(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&phy->dev->mt76.mutex);
 
-	if (!mt7915_mcu_get_rx_rate(phy, vif, sta, &rxrate)) {
+	/*
+	 * Only for a station the firmware has. mac80211 asks once more after
+	 * the station was disconnected (the last statistics of a removal), and
+	 * can ask before it is associated or, after a full reset, before it is
+	 * re-added, when its index may be another station's: a round trip for
+	 * nothing, or for someone else's rate.
+	 */
+	if (msta->wcid.sta &&
+	    !mt7915_mcu_get_rx_rate(phy, vif, sta, &rxrate)) {
 		sinfo->rxrate = rxrate;
 		sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_BITRATE);
 	}
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/main-test.c b/mt7915/tests/main-test.c
index a3cb91b8..c72ca90f 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/main-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/main-test.c
@@ -3038,6 +3038,18 @@ static void mt7915_main_test_sta_statistics(struct kunit *test)
 	msta->wcid.rate.legacy = 540;
 	mt7915_main_test_clear(fake);
 
+	/* Not associated (not yet, or disconnected for its removal, or dropped
+	 * by a full reset until it's re-added): the firmware has no such
+	 * station to ask about. The driver's own numbers are still reported.
+	 */
+	mt7915_sta_statistics(hw, vif, sta, &sinfo);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, fake->n_msgs, 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sinfo.filled &
+			   BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_RX_BITRATE));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sinfo.tx_failed, 3);
+	memset(&sinfo, 0, sizeof(sinfo));
+	msta->wcid.sta = 1;
+
 	/* the firmware sends no rate back: no rx rate */
 	mt7915_sta_statistics(hw, vif, sta, &sinfo);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt76_test_msg(fake, 0)->cmd,
